        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Earth Chimp is a good organic vegan protein on the label: about 20 g of pea, pumpkin and coconut protein in 120 calories, sweetened with monk fruit and fruit, with no gums, erythritol or added sugar, at a fair $2.21 per 25 g. Buyers like the mild taste and gentle digestion, and dislike some grit.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            What it lacks is published proof. There are no third-party certificates on its site and no sport certification, only buyer reports that the founder shares heavy metal results on request. Ask for that report, favor Vanilla or Plain over Chocolate for daily use, and watch the agave fiber if you have IBS.
